{"akin":{"w":"akin","zh":["與（……）相似"],"ipa":{"uk":"/əˈkɪn/","us":"/ʌˈkɪn/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"of kyn","t":"inh","g":"related, of kin"}],"text":"From a corruption of of kin, from Middle English of kyn (“related, of kin”), equivalent to a- + kin (1550s). Compare Old English cyn, cynn (“akin, proper, suitable”, adj.).","cog":[{"l":"ang","f":"cyn"}]}],"pos":[{"p":"adj","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"Of persons, of the same kin; related by blood.","ex":["[W]e are too near a kin to lye together, tho' vve may Lodge near one another; […]"],"grp":0},{"d":"Allied by nature; similar; partaking of the same properties; of the same kind.","ex":["Is not then Fruition near akin to Love?","She told me that she hoped my Face was not akin to my Tongue."],"grp":1,"zh":"與（……）相似"}],"forms":[["comp","more akin"],["sup","most akin"]]},{"p":"verb","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"To relate or compare; to liken.","tags":["rare","transitive"],"ex":["I like to akin the P-Diddy case to Gen-Z's version of the O.J. Simpson trial."]}],"forms":[["3s","akins"],["ing","akinning"],["pp","akinned"],["past","akinned"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"of the same kin; related by blood","zh":[],"p":"adj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:apparenté"],"it":["it:consanguineo"],"es":["es:emparentado","es:consanguíneo","es:pariente"],"pt":["pt:semelhante"]}},{"label":"of the same kind; similar","zh":["與（……）相似"],"p":"adj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:analogue"],"it":["it:affine"],"es":["es:semejante","es:similar","es:análogo"],"pt":["pt:semelhante"]}}],"lx":{"fr:apparenté":{"w":"apparenté","p":"adj","fem":"apparentée","ipa":"/a.pa.ʁɑ̃.te/","gl":"related","ety":{"chain":[]}},"it:consanguineo":{"w":"consanguineo","p":"adj","fem":"consanguinea","ipa":"/kon.sanˈɡwi.ne.o/","gl":"consanguineous","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"la","f":"cōnsanguineus","t":"der","g":"consanguineous (related by blood)"}],"text":"From Latin cōnsanguineus."}},"es:emparentado":{"w":"emparentado","p":"adj","fem":"emparentada","ipa":"/empaɾenˈtado/","gl":"of the same kin; akin","ety